`marginInfoByPosSide:` + `hotFixLever:` — the ONE-button branch.

`hotFixLever:` verbatim (`OKTASPOButtonLineVC.m:454-462`):

```objc
if (posInfo.mgnMode.length > 0) {
return [posInfo.mgnMode isEqualToString:cangModeRaw] ? posInfo.lever
: kOKTPOEmptyPlaceholder;
}
return posInfo.lever;
```

Note the nil-row path: `posInfo` nil makes `posInfo.mgnMode` nil, whose `length`
is 0, so the ObjC falls through to `posInfo.lever` — also nil. Hence
[`ArbLegLeverOutcome::NoRow`] rather than `NotApplicable` for a missing row.
